  "findings": [
    "Each successful internal READ returns IOSTAT=0, but the v4.8.0.24 branches treat zero as failure and replace the parsed coordinate/elevation with a sentinel.",
    "The transfer gate also requires ERRNUM to be nonzero even though ERRNUM contains the status of the immediately preceding elevation READ; a successful elevation read leaves it zero and blocks valid coordinates.",
    "The v4.8.5.0 comparison source uses ERRNUM .NE. 0 for the three error branches and omits ERRNUM from the coordinate validity gate."
  ],
